.nh
.TH "TEAMS" "1" "Oct 2026" "teams dev" "teams Manual"

.SH NAME
teams-post - Post a message to a channel or a chat


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBteams post  [text|-] [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Post a message.

.PP
The container is a channel (Engineering/General, a channel link or a channel
id, with --team when the reference does not name the team) or a chat (a chat
link or id, a topic name, @person or an e-mail address). A bare name is a chat
topic: a channel name is only unique inside its team, so a channel is always
written Team/Channel.

.PP
The text is markdown by default (--md), or plain text (--text) or HTML
(--html). With no text on a terminal, $EDITOR opens; \fB-\fR reads stdin. Files
(--file) are uploaded before the message is sent, and an image that fits the
4 MB inline-image limit is embedded in the message instead.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB--dry-run\fP[=false]
	print the Graph request without sending it

.PP
\fB--file\fP=[]
	file to attach (repeatable); an image up to 4 MB is embedded inline

.PP
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for post

.PP
\fB--html\fP[=false]
	send the text as HTML, sanitized against the Teams allow-list

.PP
\fB--importance\fP=""
	message importance: high or urgent (default normal)

.PP
\fB--md\fP[=true]
	treat the text as markdown (the default)

.PP
\fB--mention\fP=[]
	person to mention (repeatable); the text must name them, e.g. @alice

.PP
\fB--subject\fP=""
	subject line (channels and chats both store one)

.PP
\fB--team\fP=""
	team the channel belongs to, when the reference does not say

.PP
\fB--text\fP[=false]
	send the text verbatim, without markdown or HTML


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--jq\fP=""
	filter JSON output through a jq expression (implies --json)

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	machine-readable JSON output

.PP
\fB--no-color\fP[=false]
	disable colours (also honours NO_COLOR)

.PP
\fB--no-input\fP[=false]
	never prompt; fail fast instead

.PP
\fB--profile\fP=""
	profile to use (default: the configured default_profile)

.PP
\fB--quiet\fP[=false]
	suppress progress messages on stderr

.PP
\fB--read-only\fP[=false]
	refuse write commands

.PP
\fB--refresh\fP[=false]
	ignore cached names and resolve them again

.PP
\fB-v\fP, \fB--verbose\fP[=0]
	verbose diagnostics on stderr (-v, -vv)


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBteams(1)\fP
